  "query_preview": "..\n\nA low pressure system over eastern Wyoming will continue to\nmaintain rain showers through about 9 PM tonight, and low cloud\ncover from now through tomorrow morning is expected to remain in \nplace. This system will eventually move far enough east for cloud\ncover to begin breaking up tomorrow afternoon. A ridge is expected\nto build in from Tuesday through Friday to bring temperatures up\nto average and slightly above average. A shortwave trough will\nmove through on Wednesday to mostly affect the southeast part of\nthe area and bring rain showers. There is some uncertainty on the\ntiming of the next upper trough, but it appears more likely for \nthis to occur on Saturday and Sunday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nThe NBM typically likes to reduce PoPs quickly on the backside of\nslow moving systems, so decided to manually add PoPs through 9 PM\ntonight in the southeast. Increased winds through tomorrow\nafternoon for the higher elevation locations across the area\n(above 2500 feet). \n\nThere is high confidence in rain showers ending late this \nevening, and a ridge building in by Tuesday.\n\nThere is high confidence on a shortwave trough moving through on\nWednesday in the southeast, but there is low confidence on\nprecipitation amounts.\n\nThere is moderate confidence on a low pressure system moving in by\nFriday night.",
